@CHK
Feature: a round-trip fixture target with a coded out-of-balance feature

  A FIXTURE feature (NOT under features/) standing in for a target repo whose banked
  spec-reconciliation.json is regenerated to markdown from the JSON alone (@CLM-RMD-007).
  It names the @CHK header code (slug "checkout") and two scenarios: a
  unit-level one an attributed Vitest result balances, and an integration-level one with
  NO evidence observation — missing, so it is out-of-balance and surfaces in the
  by-feature cut named by its feature file and code. That coded out-of-balance row is what
  gives the round-trip teeth: without the feature files on the JSON (@CLM-RMD-006) the
  regenerated by-feature cut would name the bare code and DIVERGE from the direct render.

  This file lives under tests/fixtures/ (NOT features/), so this repository's own checks,
  which scan features/*.feature only, never see @CHK / @CLM-CHK-NNN.

  Rule: the fixture target names a balanced unit scenario and an out-of-balance integration scenario

    @unit @CLM-CHK-001
    Scenario: the target names a unit-level scenario an evidence observation balances
      Given the target repo's source

    @integration @CLM-CHK-002
    Scenario: the target names an integration-level scenario with no evidence observation
      Given the target repo's source
